      "content": "Demographic volatility can be measured in several ways, depending on which aspects of population change you believe affect social stability. High rates of residential turnover could indicate instability if coupled with other factors like inadequate schools or housing, while shifts in ethnic composition might reflect potential cultural conflicts or assimilation challenges. Non-citizen populations, especially if undocumented or without full integration, might contribute to tensions with local law enforcement. To quantify these factors, you can gather data on property transaction rates within different time frames, survey local populations about their perceptions of cultural diversity and community tension, and analyze the proportion and treatment of non-citizen populations in different precincts. These data points can be converted into scores or indices that reflect the level of demographic volatility in each sector, which then can be integrated into your heatmap model.",
